# Copy to bakeoff/.env and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; `.env.example` is not.
#
#     cp bakeoff/.env.example bakeoff/.env
#
# Leave a line as-is (placeholder still in <angle brackets>) to skip that arm --
# the smoke test reports it as SKIP rather than failing to parse.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. bedrock-mantle arms  (claude-sonnet-5, gemma-4-31b, nemotron-3-super-120b,
#                          kimi-k2-5)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A Bedrock API key. AWS console: Amazon Bedrock > API keys > Generate.
# Long-term keys start with "ABSK"; short-term keys are longer and expire.
AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=<paste-bedrock-api-key>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. bedrock-runtime arms  (*-runtime; SigV4-signed, needs boto3 installed)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pick ONE path and leave the other commented out. botocore prefers a named
# profile over static keys, so an AWS_PROFILE line that names a profile which
# does not exist fails with ProfileNotFound even when the keys below are valid.
# `import litellm` also runs load_dotenv() against this file, so a live line
# here reaches botocore whether or not this script parsed it.

# EITHER a named profile. AWS_CONFIG_FILE keeps the profile DEFINITION inside
# the repo too, so nothing lands in ~/.aws; relative paths resolve against
# bakeoff/. Preferred for long runs: a profile re-reads credentials per call,
# so `aws sso login` refreshes an expiring session without restarting the run.
# AWS_CONFIG_FILE=.aws/config
# AWS_PROFILE=<aws-profile-name>

# -- OR static keys. AWS_SESSION_TOKEN is required for temporary/SSO/STS
# credentials and must be omitted for long-lived IAM user keys. Temporary
# sessions expire (typically 1-12h); Bedrock reports an expired one as
# "Invalid API Key format", so preflight calls STS to name it correctly.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<paste-access-key-id>
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<paste-secret-access-key>
AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=<paste-session-token-if-temporary>

# Config pins aws_region_name: us-east-1 per arm; this is the fallback.
AWS_REGION_NAME=us-east-1
